Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00
; Substitute Times New Roman for Segoe UI and the legacy dialog font aliases.
; This is not a universal Windows font setting: coverage depends on the font name
; and rendering API each control uses. Segoe UI Variable is not mapped here.
; Requires administrator rights, and a sign-out (or reboot) to take effect.
; https://superuser.com/questions/1502897/how-to-change-the-system-font-in-windows-10
;
; Times New Roman is a proportional serif font; install it before applying this file.
; Its installed family name is "Times New Roman".
; Use the installed family name, not the product name or filename, in substitutions.
; Text outside its coverage is served by Windows' font linking / fallback.
; This substitution is intended to change the English (Latin) UI text.
;
; Two steps are needed:
;   1. unregister the Segoe UI *text* faces, so the font mapper cannot resolve the name;
;   2. add a substitution Segoe UI -> Times New Roman for font mappers that honor it.
; Segoe UI Emoji / Symbol / Historic are deliberately left registered: blanking them
; strips emoji and the symbol glyphs used by the shell.

;
; ADD
;

; 1. unregister the Segoe UI text faces (empty value = no font file)
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Fonts]
"Segoe UI (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Black (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Black Italic (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Bold (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Bold Italic (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Italic (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Light (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Light Italic (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Semibold (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Semibold Italic (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Semilight (TrueType)"=""
"Segoe UI Semilight Italic (TrueType)"=""

; 2. substitute the installed family name for Segoe UI and legacy dialog aliases
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\FontSubstitutes]
"Segoe UI"="Times New Roman"
; These aliases are independent of Segoe UI; controls requesting them need mappings too.
; Their previous values on this machine were "Microsoft Sans Serif" and "Tahoma".
"MS Shell Dlg"="Times New Roman"
"MS Shell Dlg 2"="Times New Roman"

;
; DELETE
; Restore the Windows defaults: comment out the ADD block above, uncomment the
; followings and execute. The .ttf files themselves are never touched by the tweak,
; only their registration. Restore a prior export instead if your original values differed.
;

; 1. re-register the Segoe UI text faces (the Windows 10/11 defaults)
;[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Fonts]
;"Segoe UI (TrueType)"="segoeui.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Black (TrueType)"="seguibl.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Black Italic (TrueType)"="seguibli.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Bold (TrueType)"="segoeuib.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Bold Italic (TrueType)"="segoeuiz.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Italic (TrueType)"="segoeuii.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Light (TrueType)"="segoeuil.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Light Italic (TrueType)"="seguili.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Semibold (TrueType)"="seguisb.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Semibold Italic (TrueType)"="seguisbi.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Semilight (TrueType)"="segoeuisl.ttf"
;"Segoe UI Semilight Italic (TrueType)"="seguisli.ttf"

; 2. drop the Segoe UI substitution and restore the previous legacy aliases
;[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\FontSubstitutes]
;"Segoe UI"=-
;"MS Shell Dlg"="Microsoft Sans Serif"
;"MS Shell Dlg 2"="Tahoma"
